error[E0416]: cannot assign through a `str` slice: `s` is immutable
 --> mem:///main.lu:5:5
  |
5 |     s[l-1..l] = "{t}"
  |     - this is a `str`
  |     ^^^^^^^^^ a slice of a `str` is a view, not a place
  |
  = note: a `str` never changes after it is built ([mem.str.imm]); an index or slice reads its
    bytes and cannot be written through, on any lane.
  = note: build the new text and assign it to `s`: slice the pieces out and write `s =
    "{head}{bit}{tail}"`, or `s = head + bit + tail`; `std.strbuf` is the builder for a hot
    loop.
